# The Hidden Order Behind a Sum of Products

Welcome to an interactive tour of a single, striking fact: an enormous sum of
products of binomial coefficients always collapses to **one** binomial
coefficient.

## The identity in one line

For all natural numbers $m$, $a$, $d$,
$$\sum_{i_1+\cdots+i_m=d}\ \prod_{j=1}^{m}\binom{a+i_j}{a}=\binom{ma+d+m-1}{d}.$$

Try it yourself. Move the sliders and watch a sum over many tuples become a
single term:

